&ldquo;continue,&rdquo; &ldquo;could,&rdquo; &ldquo;estimate,&rdquo; &ldquo;expect,&rdquo; &ldquo;forecast,&rdquo; &ldquo;intends,&rdquo;
&ldquo;may,&rdquo; &ldquo;will,&rdquo; &ldquo;might,&rdquo; &ldquo;plan,&rdquo; &ldquo;possible,&rdquo; &ldquo;potential,&rdquo; &ldquo;predict,&rdquo;
&ldquo;project,&rdquo; &ldquo;should,&rdquo; &ldquo;would&rdquo; and similar expressions may identify forward-looking statements, but
the absence of these words does not mean that a statement is not forward-looking. Forward-looking statements in this press release may
include, for example, the Company&rsquo;s ability to regain compliance with applicable Nasdaq standards or comply with the continued listing
standards of Nasdaq even if the Company regains compliance. These forward-looking statements are based on information available as of
